{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Let me swallow.</b> It has no parallel, and the meaning is \"feed me.\"" "And the meaning of נזיר is \"cooked dish\" only; ויזד is from the two fallen [letters] and they are two roots and the meaning is different. Likewise \"My spirit shall not judge\" (Genesis 6:3) alongside \"Nadan\" (1 Chronicles 21:27)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "Resolved דה\"א as דברי הימים א׳ (1 Chronicles); the verse citation 21:27 does not correspond to the word נדנה in the standard verse numbering of any chapter, and may reflect a different enumeration or textual corruption. The phrase \"the two fallen [letters]\" is rendered hyper-literally; it refers to a morphological argument about root letters that Ibn Ezra does not further explain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:53.926453451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}